00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:09.080
The sun was already starting to dip out of
sight behind the trees; pretty soon, it’d

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.330
be pitch black, save for the beam of his flashlight.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:17.410
He had to move fast; coyotes were only known
to attack humans on rare occasions, usually

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:21.509
they kept away, at least enough to make them
a minimal risk.

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:25.410
But waiting for him just west of the watchtower
wasn’t a coyote.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.919
At least, not at first.

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.000
Watching it from behind the tree moments later,
Ranger Holter’s stomach turned at the sight

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.000
of the creature.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.320
It walked bipedally, like a human, but the
shape was all wrong.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.350
Its legs looked broken, but that hadn’t
stopped it from catching up.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:46.570
Instead of bending at the knee, they were
Z-shaped, pointing back behind the creature,

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.630
then twisting back again in the opposite direction
at the joint.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.020
They looked more like the legs of a dog, but
they were far too big.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.530
The same could be said of its arms, bent out
of shape at multiple points like its legs

00:04:58.530 --> 00:04:59.530
were.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.000
The creature was a mess of misshapen limbs.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.699
The cartilage in its ears had seemingly reformed
into points, and there were claws protruding

00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:11.250
from its fingertips, practically bursting
out from where a human’s fingernails would

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.250
be.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.470
But beneath it all, and what alarmed Ranger
Holter the most, was its skin.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.979
It had darkened in patches, layers of fur
sprouting over those areas.

00:05:20.979 --> 00:05:28.000
But there were still parts that remained clear,
where skin – human skin – was still visible,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.340
peeling away to reveal the new, fur-coated
layer underneath.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:36.630
It looked like a grotesque accident, like
something ripped straight out of an old horror

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:42.060
movie, the kind of monster that a mad scientist
would make by haphazardly splicing DNA and

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.380
playing God.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:47.570
Holter checked the tranquilizer gun in his
trembling fingers, still empty after that

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.100
most recent shot.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:53.539
He reached for another dart, slowly sliding
it into the loading mechanism and readying

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:54.620
the pistol.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.720
It cocked… and made a sound.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.509
The creature’s malformed head turned, snapping
directly towards the source of the noise – directly

00:06:01.509 --> 00:06:02.509
towards Holter.

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:07.290
He turned to sprint away, trying to expand
the distance between him and it; if he was

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:11.210
too close, the dart wouldn’t have enough
momentum when he pulled the trigger.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:15.539
The toe of his boot snagged on something solid,
unmoving, a root from the tree he’d been

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:16.580
hiding behind.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.759
He felt himself tumble, landing with a hard
thud against the forest floor.

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:23.120
His gun, it had fallen from his grasp.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.830
He scrabbled around in the dirt for it, barely
able to see where the tranquilizer had landed

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:28.830
in the dark.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:33.039
Just as his fingertips brushed past something
metal, Holter felt the force of something

00:06:33.039 --> 00:06:35.539
heavy strike his back again.

00:06:35.539 --> 00:06:39.479
This time though, it wasn’t a tree… it
was the creature.

00:06:39.479 --> 00:06:44.530
It snarled, gnashing its canid jaws that were
protruding out from its skull, rows of sharp

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:48.919
teeth that had uprooted the old ones burying
themselves into the Park Ranger’s neck and

00:06:48.919 --> 00:06:53.020
not letting go… until he’d stopped moving
for good.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:59.069
A few short hours later, a convoy of mysterious,
unmarked vehicles arrived at Glacier National

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:00.069
Park.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:03.759
The rest of the Park Rangers who had reported
the strange activity were approached by shadowy

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:09.110
figures who refused to give their names, or
offer up any form of identification other

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:13.229
than just referring to themselves as ‘the
experts in things like this’.

00:07:13.229 --> 00:07:17.729
Not long after, none of the others would remember
Ranger Holter, or the incident that had led

00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:19.979
to his untimely death.

00:07:19.979 --> 00:07:24.819
After administering amnestics, it didn’t
take SCP Foundation search party long to discover

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:29.600
a lone coyote, sniffing around the remains
of a Park Ranger, covered in blood.

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:33.800
The wild animal was captured, to be brought
back for testing before being re-released

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:34.949
into the wild.

00:07:34.949 --> 00:07:39.720
Meanwhile, the Foundation scoured the rest
of the area until they came across the real

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.720
culprit.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:47.659
Standing in a clearing a short distance from
a footpath through the forest was SCP-1579.

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:53.000
Of course, the next challenge was getting
it packed up and transported to Bio Site 66…

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.410
without touching it.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:08:00.349
To the untrained eye, SCP-1579 looks to be
fairly unassuming, even as far as anomalous

00:08:00.349 --> 00:08:01.730
objects go.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:06.470
It is simply an old, wooden sculpture, the
kind that can even occasionally be found in

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:09.000
various wooded areas throughout the world.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:14.879
Its age is apparent from even one cursory
glance at SCP-1579, the partial damage to

00:08:14.879 --> 00:08:20.069
its cedar surface speaking to the numerous
years it has existed for, along with the bright

00:08:20.069 --> 00:08:22.250
green moss that covers it.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:27.349
Although, curiously, this moss doesn’t seem
to dry out and die in response to changes

00:08:27.349 --> 00:08:33.419
in humidity, nor does it affect SCP-1579’s
structural integrity.

00:08:33.419 --> 00:08:38.479
As for where it came from, and who made it,
those are still unknown.

00:08:38.479 --> 00:08:44.070
As if the answer to what holds SCP-1579’s
anomalous properties, whether or not the cedar

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:49.480
it was carved from or the moss coating the
sculpture possesses some unknown properties,

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:54.900
or if SCP-1579 was somehow imbued with these
after being created.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:09:01.040
Initial testing by the SCP Foundation’s
researchers determined SCP-1579 to have an

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.190
abnormally high resistance to the type of
damage wood – and particularly cedar wood

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.190
– is susceptible to.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:11.620
For one, it does not seem to show any signs
of rotting or natural degradation.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.899
For another, it is also resistant to heat
– at least, to a certain extent.

00:09:15.899 --> 00:09:20.620
It doesn’t burn the same way other objects
constructed from cedar would, however, this

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.940
sculpture is not entirely indestructible.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:29.940
Pieces can easily be chipped off of the main
body of SCP-1579, and these splintered fragments

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:35.380
continue to carry the same anomalous effects
as the rest of the sculpture, even when separate

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.380
from it.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:39.269
But, of course, you want to know about the
creature.

00:09:39.269 --> 00:09:43.440
How does this supposedly harmless – if a
little structurally abnormal – cedar wood

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.459
sculpture connects to whatever it was that
killed Park Ranger Holter?

00:09:47.459 --> 00:09:53.620
Well, it’s quite simple actually: SCP-1579
killed Holter.

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:59.250
Not directly, you understand, but by proxy
through its further anomalous properties.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.250
Still confused?

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:02.630
Well then, how about a demonstration?

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:08.240
Let’s take one of the Foundation’s preferred
test subjects, an expendable member of D Class

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:14.000
personnel, probably spending multiple life
sentences working for the SCP Foundation than

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.500
behind the bars of a maximum security institution.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:22.959
Now, what would happen if you placed this
delightful individual in the same room as

00:10:22.959 --> 00:10:24.500
SCP-1579?

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.320
Well, nothing initially.

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:31.720
That is, until the subject touches the cedar
wood surface of the sculpture, either out

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:35.870
of curiosity or following the instructions
of a Foundation researcher.

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.950
That’s when the real anomaly starts.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:43.540
The wooden sculpture will exhibit a slight,
but observable movement, shuddering slightly

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:46.329
as if moved by an unseen force.

00:10:46.329 --> 00:10:51.320
This will precede the person who touched the
object feeling a burning sensation, that kind

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:55.940
of irritating, painful heat that spreads underneath
the surface of the skin.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:11:00.020
The burning will always begin at the area
of their body that made direct contact with

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:06.610
SCP-1579, and touching it again at any point
will trigger a reactivation of the sculpture’s

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:08.220
anomalous effects.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:13.580
Subjects experiencing the effects of SCP-1579
have described the feeling as being akin to

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:18.460
a bad case of sunburn that rapidly spreads
across the skin from the point of contact,

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:22.830
only to stop once it has affected a person’s
entire body.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.890
Following the subsidence of the burning sensation,
subjects experiencing the side effects of

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:31.560
touching SCP-1579 will notice an immediate
change to their skin.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:36.870
Within a window of three minutes, their skin
becomes thin and paper-like in its texture,

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.209
before starting to peel away.

00:11:39.209 --> 00:11:44.730
Once this stage occurs, the peeling skin will
reveal a new layer underneath, hence the colloquially

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:48.320
used codename for this anomaly: ‘Different
Skin.’

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:53.190
However, this so-called different skin isn’t
merely a new layer of otherwise ordinary human

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:54.190
skin.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.910
Instead, it will belong to another species
entirely.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:03.100
A person coming into contact with SCP-1579
will find themselves rapidly developing new

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:08.380
skin that shares the physical traits – as
well as matching DNA – to that of a number

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:10.130
of animal species.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:14.320
It should be noted that these features will
continue to rapidly develop until the subject

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:20.230
is entirely transformed and is no longer considered
to qualify as a human being.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:24.620
As for the specific transformation that occurs,
there are a number of known outcomes that

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.450
repeat in the following cycle.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:32.440
Let’s say our Class D from earlier – we’ll
call them Subject A – touched SCP-1579 at

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:33.920
the start of the cycle.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:38.959
They would, after the burning sensation stops
and peeling begins, start to sprout dark feathers

00:12:38.959 --> 00:12:44.660
across their torso, arms and upper legs, likely
with a great deal of pain as the sharp quill

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.280
of these feathers start to burst out from
beneath the skin.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:52.870
Beneath the knees, Subject A will see their
legs start to become yellow and scaly, as

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:58.010
well as a change that causes their toenails
to similarly start to painfully protrude outwards

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:01.800
until they form pointed, blackened talons.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:06.170
Subject A’s face will also start to grow
feathers; however, these grow outwards away

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.610
from the areas of the nose and mouth.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:13.000
Flight feathers will also protrude from the
forearms, multiplying in number until their

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.490
entire body is covered.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:19.520
At which point, Subject A, on every level
including genetically, more closely resembles

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:26.090
a Corvus corax, more commonly known as the
common raven, than a human being anymore.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:32.550
Take another test subject, Subject B, and
get them to touch SCP-1579 right after.

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:37.339
Their different skin is covered in brown fur,
that’s approximately four inches long.

00:13:37.339 --> 00:13:41.830
Their lips and skin underneath the fur will
darken, and their nose will become constantly

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:42.899
moist.

00:13:42.899 --> 00:13:47.139
Claws will start to grow from their fingertips,
although these will be notably smaller than

00:13:47.139 --> 00:13:53.200
those of a fully grown creature of the same
species: an Ursus arctos horribilis, or a

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.550
grizzly bear.

00:13:54.550 --> 00:14:00.170
Then we get to the point in the cycle where
some unwitting hiker encountered SCP-1579

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:03.430
in the forests of Glacier National Park, Montana.

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:08.290
When this subject, Subject C, touched the
cedar sculpture, their skin began to grow

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:13.310
layered fur, as the cartilage of their ears
is separated from their tissue and replaced

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:15.930
by new, reshaped cartilage.

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:22.899
Much like Subject B, who SCP-1579 turned into
a bear, Subject C also had darkened skin,

00:14:22.899 --> 00:14:26.400
a moistened nose, and longer, sharper nails.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:31.030
It was at some point during this transformation
that an unassuming Park Ranger stumbled upon

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:36.120
Subject C. Frightened by what he saw, this
Ranger was unable to identify that what he

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:41.190
interpreted as attacks by some kind of half-human,
half-animal hybrid, were actually desperate

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:46.279
pleas for help AS Subject C was transformed
into a coyote.

00:14:46.279 --> 00:14:52.130
Although it's hard to say which physiological
change triggered by SCP-1579 is the most alarming

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:57.230
or unpleasant to experience, the fourth kind
is in no way any more pleasant than the preceding

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.860
three in the cycle.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:03.029
Subject D of this particular series of tests
will find the new layer of skin that emerges

00:15:03.029 --> 00:15:08.680
under the old to be hairless, and of a green
coloration, often with brown markings.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:13.750
Unlike the previous instances, their skin
will rapidly begin to dry out, and seems to

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:17.470
be far more reactive to the humidity of the
surrounding environment.

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:23.100
It is also far thinner than that of the skin
possessed by other transformations that SCP-1579

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.440
causes.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:29.360
So thin, in fact, that the eyeballs of Subject
D will be visible through its eyelids, which

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:34.470
rapidly become translucent, similar to those
of the Pseudacris regilla, otherwise known

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.950
as the Pacific tree frog.

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:41.850
Repeated activation of SCP-1579’s anomalous
properties will trigger the next transformation

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:46.550
in the cycle, whether the cedar wood sculpture
is touched by a new subject, or repeatedly

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.160
by the same person.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:54.040
In the latter instance, where a subject is
re-exposed to SCP-1579, the additional changes

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:57.889
their body undergoes will be significantly
more painful.

00:15:57.889 --> 00:16:02.350
Their already newly-replaced outer layer of
skin will fail to dry out, and will begin

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.430
bleeding instead.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:10.060
Three or four consecutive exposures to SCP-1579
will lead to excessive bodily trauma for the

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:14.389
subject, usually causing them to die from
shock before the fourth transformation is

00:16:14.389 --> 00:16:15.389
complete.

00:16:15.389 --> 00:16:21.199
And, as we’re sure you can imagine, an amalgamation
of a human, a raven, a grizzly bear, a coyote,

00:16:21.199 --> 00:16:24.940
and a tree frog is hardly a pleasant sight.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:29.730
This unfortunate fate was suffered during
one of the first incidents with SCP-1579 that

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:32.180
brought the Foundation’s attention to it.

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:35.750
During an elementary school field trip, a
teacher who was explaining the history of

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:40.080
totem poles in Native American culture accidentally
touched SCP-1579.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:46.140
While experiencing the pain of her transformation,
she fell against the sculpture in a panic,

00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:49.500
not realizing it had been what caused her
to change.

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:54.430
This repeated triggering of the object's anomalous
effects led to her untimely death, an event

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:58.410
that had to be wiped from the minds of her
students by the Foundation, using the careful

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.920
application of Class B amnestics.

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:06.980
For now, SCP-1579 is kept in a secure, sterile
environment at a Foundation storage warehouse,

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.890
where personnel are not permitted to make
any contact with it.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:15.240
So, there’s no need to worry about accidentally
running into SCP-1579 in the wild.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:19.799
Although, there are always plenty of other
things to worry about while out on a hike

00:17:19.799 --> 00:17:21.110
through the forest…

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:23.539
things that could be right behind you…

00:17:23.539 --> 00:17:29.960
Now check out “SCP-173 - THE SCULPTURE”
and “SCP-1897 - HUMAN DOMESTICATION SOCIETY”

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:30.460
for more!

